            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Maybe this could have a little more discussion about why?  A timeout is an unexpected error during a websocket flow.  I could see an argument that could be made for error -> warning, because it's not a fatal error, but it is unexpected in a \"correct\" context where there's no network failures.  Closing a websocket correctly should result in a canceled message here (because the connection was gracefully closed)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I could get behind WARNING here..\nWhen does it timeout ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Changed to WARNING.\nI think this websocket timeout (on async_read) might happen when GUI (e.g. obmc_console/hypervisor) may be too slow (not as responsive)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "That's a case where a warning makes complete sense to me.  This is the same thing we do on a normal http connection if the user unexpectedly disconnects.\n\nFWIW, I'm looking at the docs, and it looks like we have a 30 second timeout on connect and 300 seconds after the connection is up.\n\nhttps://github.com/boostorg/beast/blob/916dcf8eb3eff582356f7b1849446a3893da6eac/include/boost/beast/websocket/stream_base.hpp#L156\n\nIf you're hard killing the web browser, it's likely the connection isn't closing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
